cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "bvar-toolkit for Python: Python code for large Bayesian VARs"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper whose method you use
  (see CITING.md in bvar-toolkit) and this software record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Joshua C. C.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3632-128X"
    affiliation: Purdue University
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuaccchan/bvar-toolkit-python"
abstract: >-
  Python code for estimating large Bayesian vector autoregressions, the Python
  version of the MATLAB library bvar-toolkit. The functions keep their MATLAB
  names and arguments, and tests check each one against test cases exported
  from the MATLAB library, including draws made from a stream of random
  numbers shared by the two languages. Tutorials answer questions from applied
  work with the settings of a published paper, with scripts that run the same
  analysis on other data, and how-to guides show the functions at work on small
  examples with generated data.
keywords:
  - Bayesian econometrics
  - vector autoregression
  - shrinkage priors
  - marginal likelihood
  - Markov chain Monte Carlo
  - macroeconomic forecasting
  - Python
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23826635
date-released: "2026-10-30"
